          "title": "Grammar Lens: direct owner",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਸ਼ੁਰੂ (shuruu) — shurū — beginning; start."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hear and say the whole word before reading it. Keep it as a whole word rather than inventing smaller Punjabi pieces. This lesson owns the word alone; the complete instruction comes only after a separate retrieval."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "cognates",
          "title": "Across the family",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The Punjabi University dictionary records ਸ਼ੁਰੂ (shuruu) as a noun for a beginning or start. Its history reaches Punjabi from Arabic through Persian and Urdu. Keep that source history separate from present-day Punjabi use, and learn the Punjabi form as one whole. Sources: Punjabi University Punjabi-English Dictionary; Wiktionary: ਸ਼ੁਰੂ (shuruu)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
