              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਕੰਮ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਕਰੋ (kamm shuruu karo) — kamm shurū karo — start the work."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Keep the new noun whole between familiar ਕੰਮ and ਕਰੋ. Familiar ਕਰੋ carries the polite command in the already-owned noun-plus-ਕਰਨਾ pattern. Gill and Gleason describe such noun/adjective-plus-verb conjuncts as conventional combinations: this chapter teaches only this one instruction, not every possible combination, tense, or function. Source: Harjeet Singh Gill and Henry A. Gleason, Jr., A Reference Grammar of Punjabi (1969), pp. 122 and 124, conjunct verbs."
            }
          ]
        },
